-- =============================================================================
-- DROP _archive_* tables — FULLY COMMENTED; nothing executes by default.
-- =============================================================================
-- Companion runbook: docs/runbooks/post-cutover-cleanup.md
--
-- DO NOT paste this file into Railway until:
--   1. Waiting period after cutover has elapsed (see runbook).
--   2. Fresh verified backup / PITR restore point exists.
--   3. scripts/db/prod-readiness-check.sql archive sections still look healthy.
--   4. Owner explicitly authorizes the drop.
--
-- To use: copy only the uncommented DROP lines you need into a new paste,
-- after rewriting this file locally with comments removed — never leave a
-- live DROP script committed as executable SQL in this repo.
--
-- Restore notes (if you drop too early):
--   - Working-snapshot archives: restore from the pre-drop backup, then use
--     scripts/db/rollback-working-snapshot.sql only inside the safety window
--     documented in docs/runbooks/derive-synarava-state-release.md.
--   - EN translation archives: restore tables from backup, then optionally
--     scripts/db/rollback-en-translation-rows.sql.
--   - After traffic has mutated live rows, primary recovery is always the
--     verified backup — not re-deriving from stale archives.
-- =============================================================================

-- DROP TABLE IF EXISTS "_archive_product_working_snapshot";
-- DROP TABLE IF EXISTS "_archive_collection_working_snapshot";
-- DROP TABLE IF EXISTS "_archive_product_translation_en";
-- DROP TABLE IF EXISTS "_archive_collection_translation_en";
-- DROP TABLE IF EXISTS "_archive_page_translation_en";
